    "Criteria": "2.4.4 2.4.9 4.1.2",
    "Issue Description": "Links must have an accessible name.",
    "Remediation": "A link name allows screen readers to voice what the links does. If there is no link content, or the link content is hidden by CSS, screen readers have nothing to read, so read out the URL instead. To add a name do one of the following:\n\nAdd text between the a element start and end tags\nAdd an aria-label attribute\nAdd an aria-labelledby attribute\nAdd an img alt attribute labeling the link if it contains an img element",
